import{_ as t,o as s,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const p=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Script runs: an Agent's script runs in the Notebook session, and its figures stay figures","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/script-runs-episode.md","filePath":"records/script-runs-episode.md"}`),r={name:"records/script-runs-episode.md"};function n(d,e,i,h,l,c){return s(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="script-runs-an-agent-s-script-runs-in-the-notebook-session-and-its-figures-stay-figures" tabindex="-1">Script runs: an Agent&#39;s script runs in the Notebook session, and its figures stay figures <a class="header-anchor" href="#script-runs-an-agent-s-script-runs-in-the-notebook-session-and-its-figures-stay-figures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Script runs: an Agent&#39;s script runs in the Notebook session, and its figures stay figures&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Date: 2026-11-08. A follow-up to <a href="/Rho/docs/records/figure-files-episode">Figure files</a> and <a href="/Rho/docs/records/python-figures-episode">Python figures</a>, observed in three hand-driven Agent runs and then in twelve <a href="#trials">trial runs</a>, three per prompt and guidance. This is functional evidence about what the Agent did; it is not a usability claim.</p><h2 id="the-question" tabindex="-1">The question <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-question" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The question&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A figure file is readable mark by mark only while it holds the bytes a Notebook cell saved. Two files from the earlier episodes ended as pictures:</p><ul><li>Figure files run 3: Claude Code drew the corrected MA plot in the session, without a file, and wrote <code>figures/ma_plot_colored.png</code> only by running <code>Rscript scripts/ma_plot_colored.R</code> from a shell.</li><li>Python figures run 2: a cell saved <code>figures/volcano_dex.png</code> at 15:38:37; at 15:39 Claude Code ran <code>python3 analysis.py</code> from a shell, which wrote the file again with other bytes. It then said <em>Both figures are now consistent between the live Notebook and the script.</em></li></ul><h2 id="why-the-agent-ran-its-scripts-from-a-shell" tabindex="-1">Why the Agent ran its scripts from a shell <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-the-agent-ran-its-scripts-from-a-shell" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why the Agent ran its scripts from a shell&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every conversation in those episodes that wrote a script, and how it ran it (Claude Code 2.1.319, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash through workbuddy-ai):</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Episode</th><th>In the session</th><th>From a shell</th><th>Not run</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Figure files (R), 6 conversations</td><td>3: <code>source()</code> in a cell</td><td>2: <code>Rscript scripts/…R</code></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Python figures runs 2–4, 5 conversations</td><td>0</td><td>5: <code>python3 analysis.py</code> and the like, up to 4 times each</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Figure files follow-up (Python), 2 conversations</td><td>2: <code>exec(open(…).read())</code></td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The other files those shell runs wrote stayed figures only because the run wrote the same bytes a cell had saved. A cell that runs a script writes figures: <code>source(&quot;deseq2_airway.R&quot;)</code>, <code>source(…, local = dc)</code> and <code>exec(open(&quot;ma_plot.py&quot;).read())</code> each saved its files as figures.</p><p>Rho asked for the scripts. The instructions it appends to the Agent&#39;s system prompt said <em>Keep the code your results rest on in script files as well, so they can be run again without the session</em>, the Notebook&#39;s guidance said <em>Results meant to last still go to files from a script, so they can be run again without the session</em>, and the Skill <code>rho.analysis-run</code> said <em>One script written in full and then run costs less</em>. None said where to run the script.</p><p>A baseline run showed how the Agent read this. On the current guidance, with Claude Code on Westlake HPC&#39;s <code>glm-5.3-flash</code> and the Python figures prompt, it wrote <code>de_analysis.py</code>, ran it in cells and then, after the last cell, thought <em>verify the script runs standalone</em> and ran <code>python3 de_analysis.py</code> from a shell. Its answer said <em>the script also runs standalone</em>. Here the shell run wrote the same bytes as the last cell, so both files stayed figures; with any difference they would have been pictures.</p><h2 id="the-change" tabindex="-1">The change <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-change" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The change&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The three texts now ask for the script to run in the session: the system-prompt instruction, the Notebook&#39;s guidance (Notebook 0.5.13) and the Skill (<code>rho.analysis-run</code> 1.2). The scripts are still kept <em>so the results can be rebuilt without the session</em>; they are run with <code>kernel.run</code> (<code>source(&quot;analysis.R&quot;)</code> in R, <code>exec(open(&quot;analysis.py&quot;).read())</code> in Python), <em>not with Rscript or python3 from a shell: a saved figure is readable mark by mark only while its file holds the bytes a Notebook cell saved, so a shell run that writes it again leaves a picture.</em></p><h2 id="the-runs" tabindex="-1">The runs <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-runs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The runs&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Each run had its own service and disposable project, with Claude Code 2.1.319 in the Agent panel&#39;s default mode on Westlake HPC&#39;s <code>glm-5.3-flash</code> (four requests passed in 4.4 s; the user chose it after <code>deepseek-v4.1-flash</code> kept refusing the third request).</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Script runs</th><th>Other shell commands</th><th>Saved files</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Python, before (364 s)</td><td>in cells, then <code>python3 de_analysis.py</code> from a shell</td><td>30 <code>python3</code> probes, mostly of the PyDESeq2 and anndata API; <code>ls</code>, <code>head</code></td><td>2 figures (same bytes)</td></tr><tr><td>Python, after (200 s)</td><td><code>exec(open(&quot;analysis_dex.py&quot;).read())</code> in 5 cells</td><td><code>ls</code>, <code>head</code>, one <code>python3 -c</code> version check, <code>grep</code></td><td>2 figures</td></tr><tr><td>R, after (115 s)</td><td><code>source(&quot;scripts/airway_deseq2.R&quot;)</code> in 3 cells</td><td>two package checks with <code>Rscript -e</code>; <code>ls</code>, <code>mkdir</code></td><td>2 figures</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Python runs used the Python figures prompt, the R run the figure files prompt; the times are until each answer.</p><p>After the change neither run ran a script from a shell or checked one there. In R, the MA plot saved with <code>png()</code> bound all 33,469 points and the heatmap its 240 cells; the answer board showed both as figures, and the answer began <em>Everything ran in the shared R session</em>.</p><p><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/main/docs/script-runs/board-figures.png" alt="The R run&#39;s answer board: both saved files are figures"></p><h2 id="trials" tabindex="-1">Trials <a class="header-anchor" href="#trials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Trials&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>scripts/agent-trials.mjs</code> then gave each prompt to Claude Code 2.1.319 on <code>glm-5.3-flash</code> three times in parallel, on the guidance before the change (restored in a working tree) and after it. Each run had its own service and disposable project and started through the Agent panel&#39;s own operation. The runner read every transcript for script runs and shell commands, compared each saved image&#39;s bytes with the cells&#39; saved records and asked the answer board for each CSV.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Prompt</th><th>Guidance</th><th>Runs that ran a script from a shell</th><th>Saved images that are figures</th><th>CSVs previewed</th><th>Seconds</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Python figures</td><td>before</td><td>2 of 3: <code>python3 -I airway_deseq.py</code> 7 times; <code>python3 -I scripts/airway_deseq2.py</code> once</td><td>3 of 6</td><td>3 of 3</td><td>150, 516, 190</td></tr><tr><td>Python figures</td><td>after</td><td>0 of 3; <code>exec(open(…).read())</code> in 9, 2 and 2 cells</td><td>6 of 6</td><td>4 of 4</td><td>381, 221, 140</td></tr><tr><td>R figure files</td><td>before</td><td>1 of 3: <code>Rscript analysis.R</code> once</td><td>6 of 6</td><td>2 of 2</td><td>165, 170, 1,076</td></tr><tr><td>R figure files</td><td>after</td><td>0 of 3; <code>source()</code> in 3 and 5 cells, run 3 wrote its script and ran the code in cells</td><td>6 of 6</td><td>2 of 2</td><td>291, 211, 201</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Every shell run came after the cells had saved the files, to check the script &quot;standalone&quot;. In the Python run that ran its script 7 times, the standalone run failed at the volcano and then showed a clipping bug and overlapping labels, which Claude Code fixed in the script and checked only there; the volcano the person got is a picture. Both Python answers said everything ran in the shared session. The R run&#39;s shell run wrote the same bytes as its cells, so its files stayed figures. The R run of 1,076 s waited twice about five minutes on tool input the model sent that could not be parsed.</p><h2 id="also-observed" tabindex="-1">Also observed <a class="header-anchor" href="#also-observed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Also observed&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>In the Python baseline the answer board refused to preview <code>results/de_results_dex_vs_untrt.csv</code>: <em>Column names, types and null encodings must be explicit and unique.</em> pandas&#39; <code>to_csv()</code> writes the unnamed index as a column with an empty name, as R&#39;s <code>write.csv()</code> does for row names. Tables 0.5.2 (Plugins <code>ce1185f</code>) names such a column <code>row</code> (another unnamed one <code>column N</code>). The same project reopened showed the file on the answer board (<em>First 5 of 33,469 rows</em>) and in Results &amp; figures, all 33,469 rows read, with no refused request.</li><li>The instruction to explore in the session rather than with <code>python3 -c</code> or <code>Rscript -e</code> was not followed in the baseline&#39;s 30 probes, nor for the R run&#39;s two package checks.</li></ul><h2 id="not-established" tabindex="-1">Not established <a class="header-anchor" href="#not-established" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Not established&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Six runs per guidance on one model and one day. 3 of 6 runs before against 0 of 6 after is not significant at this size (one-sided Fisher exact p ≈ 0.09), and 0 of 6 still allows a rate of about 40% (one-sided 95% bound). The earlier shell runs came from another model (DeepSeek V4.1 Flash).</li><li>The baseline&#39;s 30 shell probes chased PyDESeq2 API errors that the run after the change did not hit, so the drop to one probe is not attributed to the change.</li><li>A script that only works with what the session already holds is no longer caught by a standalone run; nothing checks it now.</li><li>A file a person or a script outside Rho writes is still a picture. Rho does not tell the person why a saved figure became one.</li></ul><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Plugins <code>node --test test/kernel.test.mjs</code>: 19 of 20, 1 skipped. Plugins <code>npm test</code>: 211 of 214, 2 skipped, the U1-06d failure that predates this.</li><li>Rho <code>npm test</code>: 338 of 341, 3 skipped. All 18 CI jobs passed for <code>c46f83b0</code> with Plugins <code>24f2537</code> (run 42529798306), and for <code>ba4e9b62</code> with Plugins <code>ce1185f</code> (Tables 0.5.2, run 42532709998).</li><li>The three runs above in Chrome at 1440 px, their transcripts read for every script run and shell command, and each saved file&#39;s bytes compared with the cells&#39; saved records.</li><li>The twelve trial runs counted by <code>scripts/agent-trials.mjs</code> (its shell-script pattern was fixed to count runs with interpreter flags such as <code>python3 -I</code>, and all runs counted again), and the transcripts of the three runs that ran a script from a shell read in order.</li></ul>',30)])])}const f=t(r,[["render",n]]);export{p as __pageData,f as default};
